================================================================================
 coreboot booting inside Oracle VirtualBox 7.2.20
 via a patched DevEFI.cpp coreboot-ROM loader (CorebootRom config key)
 Firmware: coreboot emulation/qemu-i440fx, 4 MB, PAYLOAD_NONE, serial console
 Loaded with: EfiRom=coreboot.rom  +  CorebootRom=1  (COM1 captured)
 VBox.log confirmed: "EFI: coreboot image, 0x400000 bytes mapped at 0xffc00000..4GB"
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Proof points in the log below:
  - coreboot bootblock -> romstage -> postcar -> ramstage all run
  - coreboot enumerates VBox's emulated chipset:
      [8086/1237] = i440fx host bridge (VBox PIIX3)
      [8086/7000] = PIIX3 ISA
      [80ee/beef] = VirtualBox VGA
      [80ee/cafe] = VirtualBox guest-service device
      [8086/2415] = AC97 audio
 (PAYLOAD_NONE, so it stops after device enumeration -- a real payload boots on.)
================================================================================



